Crispy fried pork chops meet an addictively sticky honey garlic glaze. Center-cut pork chops are coated in an intensely aromatic dredge seasoned with ginger, nutmeg, and paprika, then fried to a golden crunch. Right before hitting the plate, each chop is drenched in a rich garlic-infused honey and soy sauce glaze that clings to every crisp ridge.

*Adapted from [Get In My Belly](http://getinmybelly.com/honey-garlic-pork-chops/).*

## Ingredients

### Pork Chops & Seasoned Crust
- 4 center-cut pork chops (bone-in or boneless, about ¾-inch thick)
- 1 cup all-purpose flour
- 2 teaspoons kosher salt
- 2 teaspoons freshly cracked black pepper
- 1 ½ tablespoons ground ginger
- 1 tablespoon ground nutmeg
- 1 tablespoon sweet paprika
- ½ teaspoon cayenne pepper
- 2 large eggs
- 4 tablespoons cold water
- Canola or peanut oil (enough to fill a skillet ½-inch deep)

### Sticky Honey Garlic Glaze
- 2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil
- 4 cloves garlic, finely minced
- 1 cup pure clover honey
- ¼ cup low-sodium soy sauce
- 1 teaspoon coarse freshly ground black pepper

## Instructions

1. **Season the Flour Dredge:** In a wide, shallow bowl or pie plate, sift and whisk together the all-purpose flour, kosher salt, black pepper, ground ginger, ground nutmeg, sweet paprika, and cayenne pepper until the spices are evenly blended throughout the flour.
2. **Whisk the Egg Wash:** In another shallow dish, beat the two eggs with 4 tablespoons of cold water until smooth and fluid.
3. **Double-Dredge the Chops:** Pat the pork chops completely dry with paper towels. Dip a chop into the seasoned flour, shaking off excess. Next, submerge it into the egg wash until fully wet, and then press firmly back into the seasoned flour, packing the spiced coating onto both sides and edges so craggy crust formations develop. Transfer to a wire rack to rest for 5 minutes while the oil heats.
4. **Heat the Skillet:** Pour high-heat oil into a deep cast iron skillet until it reaches about ½ inch up the sides. Heat over medium-high until the oil reaches 350°F (175°C), or until a pinch of flour sizzles instantly upon contact.
5. **Pan-Fry Until Crispy:** Gently lay two pork chops into the hot oil (avoid crowding the pan). Fry over medium heat for 4 to 5 minutes per side. Regulate the stovetop flame so the chops brown deeply without burning before cooking through. The pork is done when the crust is crisp and golden and a meat thermometer reads 145°F (63°C). Transfer fried chops to a wire rack set over a baking sheet to drain. Repeat with the remaining two chops.
6. **Simmer the Glaze:** While the pork fries, heat 2 tablespoons of olive oil in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Add the minced garlic and cook for 60 to 90 seconds until aromatic and softened, being careful not to let the garlic brown. Pour in the honey, soy sauce, and 1 teaspoon of coarse black pepper. Bring to a gentle boil, then lower heat and simmer for 5 to 7 minutes until the sauce reduces slightly into a glossy, amber syrup. Remove from heat.
7. **Glaze and Serve:** Use tongs to submerge each hot, crispy pork chop into the warm honey garlic sauce, turning to coat every inch of the crust. Transfer to plates and drizzle with extra spoonfuls of sauce. Serve immediately with warm Jasmine rice or buttery mashed potatoes.

## Notes

- **The Spice Blend:** The combination of ginger and nutmeg gives this breading a distinctive warm, savory profile that pairs harmoniously with the sweet honey garlic glaze.
- **Serving Tip:** Dip the chops in the glaze immediately before serving to keep the crust crunchiest.
